# Hand-written PDBx/mmCIF, not an archive entry, and the mmCIF half of a pair.
# `test/pdb_dipeptide.pdb` states the same GLY-ALA dipeptide and the same water in the legacy
# format, and `build_molecule` must return the same molecule from either.  This file states its
# intra-residue bonds and the legacy one states none, so the two exercise both sides of the
# deduplication: a `_chem_comp_bond` row and a template bond over one pair are one bond.  The
# C=O rows say DOUB, which is what the table says too -- a SING there would be the file
# contradicting the table, and the file would win.
data_DIPEP
_entry.id   DIPEP
_struct.title   'a glycyl-alanine dipeptide and one water'
#
loop_
_entity.id
_entity.type
1 polymer
2 water
#
loop_
_chem_comp_bond.comp_id
_chem_comp_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_comp_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_comp_bond.value_order
GLY N CA SING
GLY CA C SING
GLY C O DOUB
ALA N CA SING
ALA CA CB SING
ALA CA C SING
ALA C O DOUB
ALA C OXT SING
#
loop_
